Started on the tournament server in Oregon, the eighth attempt - a
variety of odd deaths, all within a few thousand turns of starting.
This game lasted 8 days in real time - currently the only Tourist
ascension. Also no geno, no poly, 56k turns - a little slow for me.

Maniac the Rambler          St:11 Dx:13 Co:18 In:11 Wi:9 Ch:15  Neutral
Dlvl:1  $:941 HP:10(10) Pw:2(2) AC:10 Xp:1/0 T:4

Started as my usual semi-pacifist, let the pet kill until my first
trip to Mine Town. DL 1 has vault sounds. DL 2 has a huge liquor
emporium - come back later. Another one on DL 3, plus the mine
entrance (lit). DL 4 has a bookstore and another vault. DL 5 has the
oracle. DL 6 has a general store.

Went into Sokoban, no problem - the wand I thought was sleep was death
:-), so the giant mimic I shot brought me to XL:2. The two pets are
both large & I came out a lot stronger with plenty of loot plus the
"oR. Still crappy armor (AC:8).

Back to the mines, ML 4 was uneventful, got to AC:6 with boots. ML 5
was also quiet. ML 7 was mine town, complete with ghost. Temple is
cross aligned, had enough loot for AC:-4. ML 9 had a couple dwarves,
left AC:-7 but bordering on burdened, made a stash. ML 12 appears to
be Mine End, I made it out with a few gray stones, will sort out
later.

Back in the main dungeon, DL 1 had about 400 Zm. The liquor stores
yielded an assortment of unidentified potions (pets), including holy
water.  DL 4 had a vault trap, brought out about 1200 Zm. DL 7 has a
vault as well as my old bones (crummy stuff...). Combined with a
leprechaun hall, another 3000 Zm and jumpiness is achieved.

DL 8 has a cross aligned altar; need a good sacrifice. Started to run
low on food; a prayer at turn 13k provided a full stomach. Of course,
I find a bones w/ four food rations soon after. A c corpse (can't eat)
shortly after provides a way to convert the altar.

DL 10 is annoying, a level teleport takes away one pet and a chameleon
turns the second into a centipede; guess I'll do without pets for a
while. Dl 12 has the entrance to the quest, at XL:10, clearly not
ready for it yet. DL 15 is a rogue level. Not sure what the deal is
with throne rooms - DL 16 has the fifth one so far. Finally got poison
resistance from a beehive on DL 17. A black pudding showed up and I
ended up with several corpses to feed on. DL 17 also has a portal to
Ludios, will pass for now. Wondered steadily down to DL 21, leaving
caches every few levels. Decided to turn around and start
consolidating stuff back on DL 8 (w/ altar) and see if I can improve
enough to take on Ludios or the Quest. (must come back to DL 16, 13,
12, 11, 10)

A sacrifice brought Giantslayer - sigh. I also got a blue glow when
holding no cursed items - double sigh. After price id'ing some books,
I get identify, slow monster, and cause fear. Identify is still 100%
fail with no metal worn. Got lucky with a blessed identify scroll -
got a lot of my stuff id'd the first time. Took quite a bit of time to
consolidate stuff, had to pray to fill my stomach again.

Got to a few caches, now have too much food (about 10 rations), and
another offering brought Ogresmasher - another sigh. Decided to clean
out the first level of the quest - not a problem at all, one wraith
taken back to the main dungeon got me to XL:14 and I qualified for the
quest.

Oh wow, on Home 3, an ogre king drank a full healing and released a
djini; that will be interesting when I start alchemy :-). Made it down
to the lowest level w/o any serious problem. Picked up a few extra
healing potions "just in case". With stealth, made it into the room
with the Master Thief and he went down to a death wand. Now going back
up. Took some time to collect all the loot and hauled it back to the
main cache on DL 8.

Some padded gloves turn out to be [oP - kept on for now. I also have a
cloak - displacement, will keep stealth for now. The one point of AC
improvement is not worth the loss. Found one of my rings is teleport
control, so I can move more easily. Grr. Another prayer got me the
castle tune, why won't you do what I want (uncurse items or a *good*
artifact)? Another prayer got stealth - I guess I can use displacement
now. Finally after about five more sacrifices, I get a blue glow and
uncurse a pile of stuff.

Start to identify stuff - have 23 identify scrolls, run through half
before I finally get a full identify. Blank a couple amnesia scrolls
and a pile of less helpful potions to make plenty of holy water. Get
better with both long sword and saber & start #twoweapon. I now have
about 30 holy water & alchemized two dozen full heals - after half of
them, I have about 220 HP, AC:-14 (from new robe & GDSM). I can
finally start to cast some spells. After a few enchantments, my
weapons are +3 and most of the armor is +4 [sigh] so so AC:-26.

Let's go check out Ludios and see how the new stuff works. Be sure to
take a levitation method as well. The new stuff works really well. My
HP did not go below 200 until I duked it out with Croseus and stayed
above 150 even then. Hauled out several piles of stuff (not armor) to
bring out along with 44K Zm. Finally got to naked AC:1, total AC:-31.

DL 24 has medusa and titan. Found a cross aligned altar on DL 23 as
well. Got teleport control finally from a tengu, can put the ring
away. Took out the titan with the wand of death. But also noting a
master mind flayer on one of the islands. It followed me somewhere
safe & my thrown daggers took it down. Medusa apparently had a amulet
of life - I had to kill it twice (one whack w/ my two main
weapons). The statues left a create monster wand and levitation
boots.

DL 25, 26 and 27 were a maze. My inventory gets full so I leave a
stash on Medusa's island. DL 28 has the castle - grr, a demi and arch
lich. I'll take it slow until they are gone. The arch lich did get a
summons in even before I left the up stairs - but went down soon
after. It also appears I have a mind flayer, couple rust monsters and
a disenchanter. A chameleon shows up and turns into a master lich -
took it down quickly as well. The worst thing was a pyrolisk - it
burnt a scroll, holy water & full healing potions before I put my
towel back on. I used the wishing wand for speed boots - decided to
save further wishes for later.

Very odd - two of the dragons had left their side hall and both side
rooms on that side were empty (except for a single long sword). I
checked the other side - food and armor were there, so something ate
all the gems and weapons?! Went on down. I may have figured out what
happened though in the VotD - a dwarf had a pile of weapons and armor
there - maybe he took it. Hmm - found a nurse in the VotD - let's see
if it is safe, Only got about 3 HP from that sequence - might not
bother the next time.

In Gehennom, DL 30 was uneventful. DL 31 had a level teleport trap -
decided to use it to go to the bottom - grr, forgot the card provides
MR. Have to figure out something later. DL 32 has Asmodeus - I paid
him 25. A stupid fire trap I hit exploded my holy water - sigh. I left
a small stock pile on this level. DL 34 has Baalzebub. Baalzebub
scowled at my 47 Zm, but went away anyway.

DL 35 has Juiblex, not a real problem, did not move or swallow - just
sat there and died. Somehow could not find the down stairs - moved to
a big area and dug down to come up later. Grr - it was hiding under a
boulder I somehow forgot to move. DL 41 has Orcus. I hit him a couple
times & he fled to the up stairs - I waited forever on the down stairs
for him to come back - then took him out on the level below. He only
got off one shot - not bad. Finally found a bag on this level - not
sure what kind it is, but its not cursed so it should be OK for now.

DL 42 turns out to have Rodney. DL 47 turns out to have the vibration
square - marked with fire Elbereth and an athame for now. Dig my
paths, do some last minute fixup, and get the invocation
artifacts. Back at the stash, AC:-37, all weapons and armor to +4 or
+5. Boosted my HP to 280 as well. My stash has plenty of gold detect
and confusion potions for the planes. Get the bell, candles, and some
extra magic mapping scrolls and go on down.

As usual, Vlad went down without too much trouble. He managed to
drink a pair of potions (healing, invisibility), but didn't even hit
me. Took a while getting out, a couple mmf's and high level liches
were generated - able to avoid mind sucking. BUC checked a few
acquired items on the altar on Orcus' level. Then level teleport to
the VS to leave the bell / candelabra, then to Rodney's tower.

Rodney went down after a couple zaps of the death wand - somehow I
kept missing. Somehow I made it through the zoo twice w/o waking every
monster up. Back to the vibration square for the invocation and go
down. A master lich showed up right away - what a pain, but I killed
it before it summoned others. Another lich decided to wake everybody
up - its fighting time. Just stood at the door to the graveyard and
kept killing monsters as they came up. After I cleaned out the
graveyard and was about to go to the next room, an arch and master
lich showed up. One managed to summon Yeenoghu and when he was killed,
he had the Amulet of Yendor - it wouldn't go into my sack - did a test
spell to be sure and it is certainly the real one. I guess I won't
visit the temple after all.

I used my cursed gain level to leave (avoiding any further Lich
encounters) and started up. Mysterious force and Rodney effects
included: 37->39, 36->38, 38->39, 39->40, 39 [Rodney], 37->38, 38->39,
34 [monsters], VotD. Apparently the RNG had it in for me for a while
:-). Dispater (peaceful) showed up just as I was leaving the Moloch's
temple on the VotD, not sure why. Then he drank a cursed gain level to
go to the Castle. In the castle, he demanded 13 Zm and scowled at 12,
very odd. It also appears that a lamp I found on the way up is magic -
still on after a long time.

More interference - 20 [black glow]. Back to the stash - time for some
final fix up. An identify there shows my lamp is oil anyway - well, it
worked while I needed it in Gehennom. A slight boost to HP (320),
refreshed some spells, and picked up the trap finding tools - off we
go. Rodney of course sent in monsters just as I was leaving, killed
one and fled the rest. Hmm. A c on DL 5, let's see if it leaves a
corpse, yes - save for Rodney on the planes. Rodney showed up on DL 1
as well - my c corpse worked just fine.

Earth - killed Rodney and the elf lord with the c corpse, the Minotaur
I killed with weapons so I could eat it (hungry). Soon after, located
the portal and with digging wand, made it over there. Air - hustled to
the right quickly, used the portal finder as soon as I could see the
right side and dodged air elementals to get there (swallowed only
once).

Fire - used the portal finder and made my way over - leading a trail
of monsters. A salamander had a death wand, I stopped to kill it and
retrieve it for my use instead of his. An archon showed up while
trying to eat a fire giant (to get to Str:18/**), decided to leave
instead. Water - took a moment to locate the portal (lower right) and
moved quickly that way. It of course moved by the time I got there so
I stayed in the bubbles for a while. Wielded the amulet to help find
my way - only took about 30 turns.

Astral - let's see - I entered on the left side, Pestilence over here,
Death in center, and Famine to right. Let's try left first. Pestilence
goes down to one death ray. Left is lawful (Blind IO), time to heal
up, turn back and try again. Not quite sure what a peaceful Angel of
the Lady is doing in a lawful temple, but it is not helping. Grr.
Someone opened the door to the temple and let Pestilence in so its
time to leave. Made it past him and locked the last door behind me.

Went to the right side. Easier to get through, but it was
chaotic. Have to do the full tour past Death now. Death didn't even
get a hit - two whacks and it went down. Grr. A full healing dropped
on Death's square, but a striking wand went boing and broke it. It
seemed to take forever to make it into the last temple, but finally
made it and the monsters started to flee.

